{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787227652492331464,"compiled_state":{"alias":"exemplary-hexahedral-needlefish","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"7cdb6c08f7d2ae9c676e6119ed038ed0ce57a27c85a6c626e05323ea3b919816","event_uuid":"5189b847-0afb-4e41-8d45-3eb3b847f38d","position":{"commit_sha":"93c726575786dc7b03be17e14ce6b2b8bc1d7aef","position":"1787209401799949001-5189b847-0afb-4e41-8d45-3eb3b847f38d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"82dc34459a749985ec0f1c97584fb845a50a51518fc21a15c35eb80f418f455e","event_uuid":"3e462722-859f-4818-9fc9-196fc6f04b16","position":{"commit_sha":"494c23eeeace86dfdee7d98da869f3d21f650622","position":"1787209426572402001-3e462722-859f-4818-9fc9-196fc6f04b16"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f5b1206458e782b960df9589d0748744a574704b58232d23011cb41ab0ccc5d3","event_uuid":"4deba645-54ed-4109-8035-8c84a46c1cab","position":{"commit_sha":"afb0806b16ffe119b48aca2ef4a6d437d54487a3","position":"1787209436743266001-4deba645-54ed-4109-8035-8c84a46c1cab"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787209401799949001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"3e462722-859f-4818-9fc9-196fc6f04b16","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ea16-dd54-3a8f-4293"},{"link_uuid":"4deba645-54ed-4109-8035-8c84a46c1cab","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"baeb-4f4b-3227-457e"}],"description":"## Problem\nDuplicate tickets are being filed for work that already exists, and the duplication is only\ndiscovered when an agent has already been dispatched and is mid-implementation. The cost is a full\nagent's investigation each time.\n\n**Twice in one session (2026-08-19/20):**\n\n1. `elfish-saltwater-pika` (ea16-dd54) — \"Land dependabot PRs #129 + #130 as one Gerrit change\".\n   An agent was dispatched, did the verify-first analysis, and found the ENTIRE scope had already\n   landed ~2.5 hours after the ticket was created, under a DIFFERENT ticket with the SAME TITLE:\n   `woodblock-gnatty-xiaosaurus` (5a90-ec98), Gerrit 1832, merged 2026-08-17. Closed as a duplicate;\n   no code was needed. That agent's time was spent entirely on discovering the duplication.\n\n2. `decagonal-indisposed-tamarin` (baeb-4f4b) — \"Shrink test-only real-time windows in subprocess and\n   network sentinels\". The implementing agent's overlap detector flagged it as a duplicate of the\n   already-closed `039b-d179-b669-4439` — same title, same two files, landed as `a79ed876b0`. That\n   agent salvaged the situation by rewriting the plan to cover only the RESIDUAL work left on main,\n   so the change was still worth landing — but it discovered this only after claiming and planning.\n\nIn both cases the duplicate carried the SAME TITLE as the original. That is the cheapest possible\nsignal and it was not acted on at creation time.\n\n## What already works, and where the gap is\nrebar HAS an overlap detector, and in case (2) it fired correctly — the implementing agent saw the\n`duplicates` relation surfaced during its work. So detection exists; the gap is WHEN it runs.\nToday it surfaces at claim/plan time, by which point an agent is already dispatched and paying for\nthe investigation.\n\nThe obvious question to answer first: does `rebar create` consult that same detector? If it does and\nthese still slipped through, the detector's sensitivity is the issue. If it does not, wiring it in is\nthe fix. Establish which before designing anything.\n\n## A concrete secondary defect found while handling case (2)\n`rebar link <source> <target> duplicates` is REFUSED when the SOURCE ticket is closed. The agent in\ncase (2) could not record the duplicate relation at all and had to leave it in a comment, where no\ntooling can see it.\n\nThat is backwards for this use: recording that a closed ticket duplicated another is exactly the\nbookkeeping you want to be able to do after the fact. Note the close gate has the mirror-image rule\nand gets it right — closing with `--class duplicate` REQUIRES a `duplicates` link and explicitly\nsays \"the replacement ticket may already be closed — the gate requires only that the link exist,\nnever that its target still be open.\" The link command should be equally permissive about the\nsource's status, or at least offer a sanctioned way to record the relation post-close.\n\n## Why this is worth fixing rather than tolerating\nThe failure is self-concealing. A duplicate ticket looks exactly like real work: it has a title, a\nplan, acceptance criteria, and it passes plan review. Nothing about it signals \"this is already\ndone\" until someone reads the store or the code. So the cost is not a small tax — it is a full\ninvestigation cycle, repeated for every duplicate, and it scales with how many agents are working\nthe queue in parallel. This session ran five concurrent agents; the exposure is proportional.\n\nThere is also a correctness risk beyond wasted time: case (1)'s agent noted that re-applying the\nalready-landed dependency pins would have ACTIVELY FOUGHT a newer upstream PR. A duplicate that gets\nimplemented rather than detected can undo newer work.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Establish and record whether `rebar create` currently consults the overlap detector, with the\n      file and line that does or does not.\n- [ ] A ticket whose title matches an existing ticket's is SURFACED at creation time — the author is\n      told, with the candidate ticket's id and status. Proven by creating a same-title ticket in a\n      test and asserting the signal appears. Title match is the minimum bar; both real cases would\n      have been caught by it.\n- [ ] The signal does not block creation. Legitimate same-title tickets exist (follow-ups, retries,\n      per-environment variants); the requirement is that the author is INFORMED, not prevented.\n- [ ] `rebar link <closed-source> <target> duplicates` is permitted, or a sanctioned alternative\n      exists for recording a duplicate relation after the source is closed. Whichever is chosen,\n      `elfish-saltwater-pika` and `decagonal-indisposed-tamarin` end up with machine-readable\n      `duplicates` links rather than prose comments.\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass; `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check`\n      reports `new=0 increased=0 stale=0`.\n\n## Provenance\nBoth incidents observed directly during the 2026-08-19/20 triage session; ticket ids, Gerrit change\nnumbers and merge shas above are from the agents' own reports and were not inferred.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","baeb-4f4b-3227-457e"],["relates_to","ea16-dd54-3a8f-4293"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"eac3-ed70-764a-4f9e","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Duplicate tickets are only detected after an agent is mid-implementation; same-title collisions pass creation unflagged","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["5189b847-0afb-4e41-8d45-3eb3b847f38d","3e462722-859f-4818-9fc9-196fc6f04b16","4deba645-54ed-4109-8035-8c84a46c1cab"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787227652492331464,"uuid":"083a107f-60a7-40d4-9a17-b5390e468133"}